  "generated_text": "1. We need to choose 3 classes out of 8.\n2. This is a combination problem, where the order of selection does not matter.\n3. The formula for combinations is \\( \\binom{n}{r} = \\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} \\).\n4. Here, \\( n = 8 \\) and \\( r = 3 \\).\n\nSo, we calculate:\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{3} = \\frac{8!}{3!(8-3)!}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8!}{3! \\cdot 5!}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8 \\times 7 \\times 6 \\times 5!}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 5!}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8 \\times 7 \\times 6}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{336}{6}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 56\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways Michael can choose 3 out of 8 math classes is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{56\n}",
